  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000020",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The reaction of sodium bromide and concentrated sulfuric acid is:",
    "reading_order" : 20,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000021",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**H**<sub>**2**</sub>**SO**<sub>**4 **</sub>**(l) + NaBr (s) → HBr (g) + NaHSO**<sub>**4 **</sub>**(s)     **",
    "reading_order" : 21,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000022",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The concentrated sulfuric acid **oxidises **HBr which decomposes into **bromine **and **hydrogen gas **and sulfuric acid itself is **reduced **to **sulfur** **dioxide** **gas**:",
    "reading_order" : 22,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000023",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**2HBr (g) + H**<sub>**2**</sub>**SO**<sub>**4 **</sub>**(l) → Br**<sub>**2 **</sub>**(g) + SO**<sub>**2 **</sub>**(g) + 2H**<sub>**2**</sub>**O (l)**",
    "reading_order" : 23,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
